From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quill <siinspam@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:31:45 +0000
Subject: fix(nako): rebrand compatibility

The rebrand renames everything that carries the upstream name. Two things
outside the fork still use it and broke.

Installs: from 6.0 eslint-plugin-react-hooks depends on two outside parser
packages whose names carry the upstream brand. The rebrand renames them and
the registry has no such packages, so every install failed fetching Node
dependencies. Pin 5.2.0, which has no such dependency and keeps
rules-of-hooks and exhaustive-deps; the web config drops the rules only 7.x
provides.

Plugins: the rebrand renames the core packages, their helpers and the
environment variables, so every plugin written for upstream failed at its
first core import. Serve the upstream module names as the real modules,
resolve upstream-spelled attributes on them, and read an upstream-spelled
environment variable from its renamed one. A build that kept the upstream
name is unaffected.

Co-authored-by: Nako <nako@quill.moe>

